     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><font size=\"3\">Hi! </font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><font size=\"3\">Make a map with ggplot2 and I would like to\r\nbe able to adjust the scale of the coordinated axes conveniently.</font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"> </span>In\r\nmy case, I need to define the scale on the axis x as follows: -67.2, -67.4,\r\n-67.6... The code <span style=\"margin:0px\"> </span>used is the following:\r\n</font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><font size=\"3\">ggplot () + geom_point (aes (x = Length, y\r\n= Latitude, color = data), size = 4, alpha = 1) + scale_colour_gradientn\r\n(colors = t (tim.colors (100) )) + Geom_path (aes (x = PRborder [, 1], y =\r\nPRborder [, 2]))</font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"> </span>If\r\nanyone has any suggestions? </font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><font size=\"3\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Greetings and thanks</span></font><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\"> </font></font><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
